1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,426
Your own systems can read the units

2
00:00:02,426 --> 00:00:04,851
you promote to, through the promoter API.

3
00:00:04,851 --> 00:00:07,623
In the promoter portal, open the Developer
tab.

4
00:00:07,623 --> 00:00:11,088
Select Create key, name it Production
sync, and select Create.

5
00:00:11,088 --> 00:00:14,900
The full key is shown now, and only now:
Miftah keeps

6
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,365
a fingerprint of it and can never show it
again.

7
00:00:18,365 --> 00:00:20,790
Select Copy, put it in your secret

8
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:22,869
manager, then select I've saved it.

9
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:26,681
The key is listed as Active, by its first
characters only.

10
00:00:26,681 --> 00:00:30,839
On your server, every call sends the key
in the X-Api-Key header.

11
00:00:30,839 --> 00:00:33,958
Ping checks that the key works, and
answers with

12
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:36,730
the promoter and the organisation it acts
for.

13
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:39,848
Units count is the cheap call: two
properties, eight

14
00:00:39,848 --> 00:00:42,620
units, and a fingerprint of the whole
list.

15
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:46,432
Units returns the list itself, a page at a
time: each

16
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:49,897
unit's ID and number, and its property's
ID and name.

17
00:00:49,897 --> 00:00:53,015
Nothing about tenants, contracts or
payments is ever included.

18
00:00:53,015 --> 00:00:55,094
Every page carries the same fingerprint.

19
00:00:55,094 --> 00:00:57,867
That fingerprint keeps your copy in sync
cheaply.

20
00:00:57,867 --> 00:00:59,946
Every fifteen minutes, call units count.

21
00:00:59,946 --> 00:01:03,757
If the fingerprint is the one you stored,
nothing has changed.

22
00:01:03,757 --> 00:01:06,529
If it differs, fetch every page of units

23
00:01:06,529 --> 00:01:08,955
and replace your list in one step.

24
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:11,380
Now let the coupon carry the unit.

25
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:13,459
Open Ads and edit the coupon.

26
00:01:13,459 --> 00:01:15,538
Its link already passes the code.

27
00:01:15,538 --> 00:01:17,964
Select Add parameter: unitId, from Unit
ID.

28
00:01:17,964 --> 00:01:20,043
Add another: propertyId, from Property ID.

29
00:01:20,043 --> 00:01:22,815
Tenants are asked before their details are
shared,

30
00:01:22,815 --> 00:01:25,240
and the example shows the finished link.

31
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,052
Save, and the ad goes back to an
administrator for approval.

32
00:01:29,052 --> 00:01:33,210
On the tenant's phone, they tap Copy and
the code is copied.

33
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:37,368
Because the link carries their unit, they
are asked to agree first.

34
00:01:37,368 --> 00:01:40,487
Then the phone itself opens the https
link: in

35
00:01:40,487 --> 00:01:43,605
your app, if it has verified Universal
Links or

36
00:01:43,605 --> 00:01:46,724
App Links for your domain, otherwise on
your website.

37
00:01:46,724 --> 00:01:48,456
Custom app schemes are refused.

38
00:01:48,456 --> 00:01:50,882
Once the ad is approved again, a

39
00:01:50,882 --> 00:01:52,961
tenant in A-102 opens this link.

40
00:01:52,961 --> 00:01:57,119
Take the unitId and look it up in your
synced units: it

41
00:01:57,119 --> 00:02:00,931
is A-102 in Oasis Crest Residence Tower,
one of your units.

42
00:02:00,931 --> 00:02:03,356
An ID that is not in your

43
00:02:03,356 --> 00:02:05,435
list is not one of yours.

44
00:02:05,435 --> 00:02:08,207
Whether a code was already used is your

45
00:02:08,207 --> 00:02:10,633
own rule: Miftah does not track
redemptions.

46
00:02:10,633 --> 00:02:13,405
To replace a key without downtime, select
Rotate.

47
00:02:13,405 --> 00:02:16,523
The new key is shown once, like the first.

48
00:02:16,523 --> 00:02:19,642
The old key is now Expiring: it keeps
working

49
00:02:19,642 --> 00:02:22,760
for twenty-four hours while you move your
servers over.

50
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:26,226
When everything uses the new key, revoke
the old one.

51
00:02:26,226 --> 00:02:30,037
The reason is optional, and the key stops
working at once.

52
00:02:30,037 --> 00:02:33,156
If a key leaks, Miftah can stop it too.

53
00:02:33,156 --> 00:02:36,967
A super admin opens API keys and pastes
the leaked key

54
00:02:36,967 --> 00:02:40,779
into the search, which finds that one key
in any organisation.

55
00:02:40,779 --> 00:02:44,590
Select Revoke, give the reason, which is
required here, and confirm.

56
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:47,362
Back in the Developer tab, the key shows

57
00:02:47,362 --> 00:02:49,788
Revoked by Miftah admin, with that reason.

58
00:02:49,788 --> 00:02:52,560
Create a new key whenever you need one.
